# Stable, platform-independent line-ending behaviour for evidence files.
#
# Every frozen/derived evidence file (raw model-output JSONL, review/report
# CSVs) is stored in the git object database with LF line endings and is
# checked out with LF on every platform, regardless of a contributor's local
# core.autocrlf setting. This does NOT change any record's content or order --
# it only pins the newline byte sequence so that a SHA-256 taken from a Linux
# clone and a SHA-256 taken from a Windows clone of the same commit are
# comparable without a line-ending-conversion false positive. See
# docs/final_audit/FROZEN_ARTIFACT_HASHES.csv (repository_sha256 vs
# canonical_text_sha256 vs original_windows_crlf_sha256) for how this is
# reconciled against pre-existing Windows-checked-out working trees.
*.jsonl text eol=lf
*.csv text eol=lf

# Everything else: let Git auto-detect text vs binary, normalise text files to
# LF in the repository, but do not force a particular checkout line ending.
* text=auto

# Explicitly binary: never apply any line-ending or diff conversion.
*.zip binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.7z binary
*.rar binary
